course: dictionary
lesson: 8581
title: Schoolwork
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Schoolwork is the work pupils do for school. It can happen in lessons or at home. Reading, writing, maths exercises, projects and homework are all schoolwork. «Asking for help with schoolwork is a strong thing to do, not a soft one.»
explain: Schoolwork is uncountable, so you say a lot of schoolwork, not two schoolworks. Some useful phrases are do your schoolwork, help with schoolwork and keep up with schoolwork.
explain: Looking after yourself counts too. Balance schoolwork with play and rest. «It wasn't: he spent the days doing schoolwork at his gran's, missed the planning for the class trip, and came back behind in maths.» Falling behind is what happens when schoolwork is missed, so keep up with it.
fact: Schoolwork means the work that pupils do for school, in lessons or at home.
fact: Schoolwork is a noun, and it is uncountable: you cannot say "two schoolworks".
fact: Reading, writing, maths exercises, projects and homework are all schoolwork.
fact: If schoolwork feels too hard, ask for help. This is a sensible thing to do.
fact: «Hiding that you do not understand schoolwork makes the gaps bigger and harder to fix later.»
exercise: «Asking for help with schoolwork is a strong thing to do, not a soft one.» What is schoolwork? | Only the tests you sit at the end of term | Games played at break time | *Work that pupils do for school, in lessons or at home | A holiday away from school
exercise: Which of these is schoolwork? | Watching TV after tea | Playing football at break | *Writing a story and doing maths exercises | Sleeping in on a Saturday
exercise: «A suspension is not a holiday; the pupil still has to do schoolwork and falls behind.» What does this sentence tell you? | Schoolwork stops completely during a suspension | Schoolwork only happens at weekends | A pupil can skip all schoolwork during a suspension | *A pupil still has to do schoolwork, even when away from school
test: Which phrase means to stay level with your schoolwork and not fall behind? | Keep out of school | *Keep up with schoolwork | Give up schoolwork | Ask for lunch
test: Which sentence uses schoolwork correctly? | I have two schoolwork tonight | *I have a lot of schoolwork tonight | I have an schoolwork tonight | I have many schoolworks tonight
exam: «Hiding that you do not understand schoolwork makes the gaps bigger.» What should you do instead? | Stop doing schoolwork altogether | Wait until the exam | *Ask for help early | Hide it even more
